    <string name="time_story_wright_fourth">On the day of their first successful powered flight, the Wright brothers’ fourth flight lasted 59 seconds.</string>
    <string name="time_story_bannister_duration">3 minutes 59.4 seconds</string>
    <string name="time_story_bannister">In 1954, Roger Bannister ran a mile in 3 minutes 59.4 seconds, becoming the first person to break the four-minute barrier.</string>
    <string name="time_story_shepard_duration">15 minutes 22 seconds</string>
    <string name="time_story_shepard">In 1961, Alan Shepard’s first spaceflight took 15 minutes 22 seconds from launch to splashdown.</string>
    <string name="time_story_white_duration">About 23 minutes</string>
    <string name="time_story_white">In 1965, Ed White began his spacewalk above the Pacific near Hawaii. About 23 minutes later, it ended above the Gulf of Mexico.</string>
    <string name="time_story_ganna_duration">1 hour</string>
    <string name="time_story_ganna">In 2022, Filippo Ganna cycled 56.792 kilometres on an indoor track in a single hour.</string>
    <string name="time_story_gagarin_duration">1 hour 48 minutes</string>
    <string name="time_story_gagarin">In 1961, Yuri Gagarin’s journey as the first human in space lasted 108 minutes.</string>
    <string name="time_story_tennis_duration">11 hours 5 minutes</string>
    <string name="time_story_tennis">At Wimbledon in 2010, Isner and Mahut played one match across three days. Playing time alone added up to 11 hours 5 minutes.</string>
    <string name="time_story_beatles_duration">1 day</string>
    <string name="time_story_beatles">On 11 February 1963, the Beatles recorded ten of the fourteen tracks for their debut album, Please Please Me, in one day.</string>
    <string name="time_story_lindbergh_duration">33 hours 30 minutes</string>
    <string name="time_story_lindbergh">In 1927, Charles Lindbergh flew alone and nonstop from New York to Paris. Crossing the Atlantic took 33 hours 30 minutes.</string>
    <string name="time_story_gemini_duration">About 4 days</string>
    <string name="time_story_gemini">In 1965, the two astronauts aboard Gemini IV spent about four days in Earth orbit.</string>
    <string name="time_story_apollo_duration">About 8 days 3 hours</string>
